// Parallax depth on Showhome (src/map_materials.rs): the art kit's depth maps (src/showhome_kit.rs, heights from
// the kit's v2 texture manifest) and the ground's relief (src/showhome_ground.rs, assets/shaders/showhome_ground.wgsl).
(
    // Per VIDEO quality PRESET. `layers`: steep-parallax steps at a grazing view (1 looking straight at the face);
    // 0 turns parallax off (LOW: the surfaces look and cost as without it, and the kit's height images are not
    // even loaded until a higher preset asks for them). `relief_steps`: binary-search steps that refine the hit
    // (relief mapping: sharp joints, no stair steps). Every enabled preset uses relief mapping so a preset change
    // never compiles a new shader variant; only the step counts (uniforms) change. Every step is one depth-map
    // sample per pixel on these surfaces.
    quality: (
        low: (layers: 0, relief_steps: 0),
        medium: (layers: 8, relief_steps: 2),
        high: (layers: 12, relief_steps: 4),
        ultra: (layers: 20, relief_steps: 6),
    ),
    // The ground's relief marches `steps_per_px` steps per pixel that its deepest shift spans on screen (at most
    // the preset's `layers`), and none where that shift is under `min_px` pixels: up close it marches the
    // preset's full count, farther out (and seen from above) only what can still move a pixel. So a step never
    // moves the picture by more than a pixel (with 1 per pixel), wherever the full count would have.
    ground: (steps_per_px: 3.0, min_px: 0.5),
)
